            "command": "cd /home/leon0399/Projects/llame; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport re\nsrc=open('openspec/specs/chat-search/spec.md').read()\ndef req(name):\n    m=re.search(r'(### Requirement: '+re.escape(name)+r'\\n.*?)(?=\\n### Requirement: |\\Z)',src,re.S)\n    return m.group(1).rstrip()+'\\n'\nrank=req('Results are ranked by fused relevance with canonical model shaping')\nold=(\"The web response contract (`id`, nullable `title`, nullable `snippet`, `updatedAt`) and current `search_conversations` input schema (`query`, `limit`) SHALL be preserved until #198 intentionally replaces the model tool input.\")\nassert old in rank\nnew=(\"The web response contract (`id`, nullable `title`, nullable `snippet`, `updatedAt`) SHALL be preserved. The `search_conversations` model input SHALL be the strict two-mode contract defined below; the prior `{ query, limit }` shape SHALL NOT be accepted or aliased.\")\nrank=rank.replace(old,new)\nold2=\"Later reshaping of this result is #198's decision.\"\nassert old2 in rank\nrank=rank.replace(old2,\"This anchor is retained unchanged by the timeline-and-range contract; its interaction with a required range is defined below.\")\n# insert the new contract paragraphs before the first scenario\nfirst_sc=rank.index('#### Scenario:')\ncontract='''`search_conversations` SHALL accept exactly one strict object with unknown properties rejected: `mode` (`content` or `timeline`), optional `query`, optional `after` and `before` (absolute timezone-explicit instants forming the half-open interval `[after, before)`), optional `constraint` (`required` or `preferred`), and optional integer `limit`. In `content` mode `query` SHALL be present and non-blank, `constraint` SHALL be present when any bound is present and absent otherwise, and `limit` SHALL be 1–10 with default 5. In `timeline` mode `query` and `constraint` SHALL be absent, at least one bound SHALL be present, and `limit` SHALL be 1–50 with default 20. When both bounds are present `after` SHALL be strictly earlier than `before`. A bound MAY be omitted on either side; a missing bound imposes no clause and SHALL NOT be silently filled with the current instant. Every violation — unknown field, blank query, missing query, query or constraint in timeline mode, no bound in timeline mode, bound without constraint in content mode, reversed or empty range, malformed instant, out-of-range limit — SHALL return a bounded invalid-argument observation before any retrieval statement executes. The tool SHALL NOT parse natural-language dates.\n\nA `required` range SHALL exclude candidates whose canonical eligible message timestamps fall outside `[after, before)` before ranking, and a resolved content passage whose own message timestamp falls outside the range SHALL be omitted after hydration even when its projection document overlapped the range. A title-only candidate under a required range SHALL be returned as `kind: \"metadata\"` only when the Chat has at least one eligible message inside the range. A `preferred` range SHALL NOT exclude any candidate; it SHALL add one bounded additive rank-fusion contribution — no greater than the contribution a document earns by ranking first in a single leg — to documents whose message timestamps fall inside the range, so a strong match outside the range remains retrievable in its ordinary position relative to clearly weaker in-range matches and carries its actual timestamp. With no range, content mode SHALL preserve the global relevance order and SHALL NOT apply a recency decay.\n\nEvery success SHALL carry an envelope with the closed untrusted-history notice, `appliedRange` echoing exactly the bounds and constraint received (an omitted bound is absent), and `truncated: true` when at least one further qualifying result existed beyond `limit`. Per-leg ranks, fused scores, matched-by legs, and the reason a candidate was omitted SHALL NOT appear in any row or in the envelope.\n\n'''\nrank=rank[:first_sc]+contract+rank[first_sc:]\nrank